"token token" style="color: rgb(112, 184, 255);">add</span><span> </span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(251, 173, 96);">.</span><span>
</span></span><span><span></span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(112, 184, 255);">git</span><span> commit -m </span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(155, 233, 99);">"Add device-side ESP32 firmware code"</span><span>
</span></span><span><span></span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(112, 184, 255);">git</span><span> push origin main</span></span></code></pre></div></div>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">After that your repo will have both your <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">server/</code> work and his <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">device/</code> work in one place — which is exactly what the project requires.</p>
